in italy we have a famous song  in case the world is falling down i go  back a little bit to not get hurt but  what if a nuclear bomb were to fall in  the city where i live in tuscany which  is prato this is something i ask myself  with a bit of paranoia how much further  back am i supposed to go to ensure that  i don't vaporize instantly after all the  dogma of this era seems to be never say  never pandemics wars italy out of the  world cup meanwhile everyone wants to  build their own bunker yep there are  companies that are specialized in this  now you know in switzerland just to say  since 1963  it is mandatory by law to provide every  building with a bomb shelter while in  italy we don't have any regulatory plan  providing for the construction of  bunkers at least in theory but hey  what's the deal we can always use our  sellers as bunkers after getting all the  permissions of course  if you had a thousand years the door is  now closing guys however since a bunker  costs several tons of thousands of  dollars and since i'm not paid enough if  an atomic bomb were to follow my little  town i would have no choice but to run  away hopefully with a fast car luckily  for me a simulator called nuke map  created by historian alex wallerstein  has been around for several years now  showing the range of action and  destruction of an atomic device  [Music]  we'll take a look at it but before i  give you an unjustified anxiety i wanted  to ask myself what are the nations that  possess the warheads capable to unleash  the atomic holocaust  these are not so many on the one hand  you have the classic ones united states  russia france the united kingdom china  which are all signatories of the treaty  on the non-proliferation of nuclear  weapons but on the other hand you have  four countries that are not yet members  of such agreement namely india pakistan  north korea and israel even if the  latter is only unofficially part of it  apart from a couple of them they all  seem to be nice and quiet but surprise  we italians still have nuclear warheads  at our disposal oh right they are not  really ours according to the nato  nuclear sharing plan it has been decided  to involve in the nuclear warfare also  some non-nuclear countries of the  alliance like us italians mostly for  shared strategies and planning but also  for the supply of warheads so much  non-proliferation  i can smell it the u.s and who otherwise  have land italy belgium germany the  netherlands and turkey their own toys  that of course they cannot use at their  own pleasure so did you hear me don't  play with those gifts the bombs are  guarded by u.s soldiers and without us  codes they can't be used but in case of  war we still have to prove that we're  capable of using them and we cannot  afford to fall off the wagon according  to a report by analyst hans christensen  from the nature resources defense  council in 2005 in italy there were 90  warheads 50 in the base of aviano and 40  in the base of geditory today the  estimates point a total of 40 warheads  but it seems also that there's a real  secret bilateral agreement between our  country and the u.s called stone x which  would provide for a further deployment  of american nuclear weapons on our  territory making an estimates of the  warheads currently in circulation is a  bit complicated but one thing is certain  russia and the united states share about  90 percent of the world's nuclear  weapons according to the federation of  american scientists in the first part of  2022 the estimated number of warheads  around the world was 12  700 of these except those being  dismantled the actual warheads for  military use are  9400 but only 3700  are the ones currently deployed and  operational 2000 of these even in state  of alert ready for immediate use russia  would be in the first place with  5977 warheads followed by the united  states with 5428  but if we take into account only the  deployed warheads the united states  would have a slight advantage 1744  against 1588.  just to realize the difference in level  with the rest of the world in third  place we find china which boasts only  350 warheads while north korea only has  20 warheads yes dr kim you have to eat  more uranium we should go easy on good  old kim apparently he has some very  dangerous new toys now in fact  pyongyang's latest tests have glorified  the power of the new wazon 17 missiles  capable of reaching american and  european soil  these images from north korean state  media show the country launching its  most powerful missile yet  inside the isolated and secretive  country celebration  of course so far they haven't gone  beyond japan a coincidence one might say  north korea is provoking the  international community even as it's  responding to russia's invasion of  ukraine  we absolutely cannot tolerate this okie  dokie potentially kim could hit us right  now if he wants what about the others  france would have no problem at all to  hit their beloved cousins from italy and  since in the past they have already  given us their warheads i would be  careful also usa and uk may have no  problem to send us their missiles and  neither russia pakistan and india  perhaps wouldn't make it both the  pakistani shaheen and the indian agni  have a more limited range after all they  only care about destroying each other  and maybe hitting china china for its  part with its d41 missiles and  especially with the new hypersonic  models has all the requirements to be a  good candidate to destroy my town in  tuscany come on bring it on you and what  are me  [Music]  they sound convincing so what would  happen if a nuclear warhead fell right  here in this exact spot where i live  let's say for example a russian warhead  hits the ground right here purely random  example first of all according to the  experts of the bulletin of the atomic  scientists it's also to be believed that  the nuclear warheads today at the  disposal of the russians have a charge  of 100 kilotons which to be clear would  be equivalent to 800 000 tons of  dynamite those of hiroshima and nagasaki  were between 15 and 20 kilotons  intercepting a nuclear intercontinental  ballistic missile is technically  possible but very difficult and  unpredictable given the parabolic  trajectory of the icbm the most basic  system is basically just shooting a  missile at a missile yes during the cold  war that's what russians and americans  called anti-ballistic missile but we  never had the honor to experiment the  effectiveness of such tactics so far  hiroshima and nagasaki were the only two  history cases of nukes dropped on  civilians and japan didn't have any  anti-ballistic missile system at the  time the idea would be to hit the icbm  and make it blow up somewhere other than  its intended target this with all the  consequences it may have on the  atmosphere anti-ballistic systems are  present in various countries and are  still under full development nowadays  india's abm system is capable of  intercepting missiles up to 2 600  kilometers and potentially to 5 000  kilometers but in a worse scenario no  one has activated their own defense  system yet  in report by the american physical  society panel on the public affairs even  the americans seems to have a limited  capability to intercept an  intercontinental ballistic missile in  the study it is stated the current  capabilities are low and will likely  continue to be low for the next 15 years  to protect the us against a strike from  north korea we are speaking about 20  warheads regarding north korea imagine 6  000 russian nukes goodbye source  proposed by the us administration the  ground-based mid-course defense also  known as gmd is operational in both  alaska and california and provides more  protection against the nuclear threat  from north korean missiles or launches  from russia or china but it's likely  less effective against missiles launched  from the middle east here in italy we 