me long lasting disputes with  those in pistolia we don't love each  other very much in case you're luckier  than me you could always live near a  large public fallout shelter the  luckiest ones in italy live in the  province of verona in afi where there's  the largest bunker of its kind in our  country located in the bowels of mount  moscow built in the 60s to house a nato  command post the bunker is thirteen  thousand square meters wide and can  accommodate almost one thousand people  once upon a time it was well stocked but  for some years now it has been  dismantled and it's now almost unusable  you can also try to be lucky entrentino  under mount mice in valdenon where you  will find the gumpen bunker  being bombed during world war ii our  country has hundreds if not thousands of  shelters from private to public ones in  nearby florence you could look for one  of the many city shelters built to  escape from the bombings from the  undergrounds of the basilica of  salorenzo to palazzo vecchio if you  found yourself in florence during a  nuclear attack observe on the walls the  presence of an r indicating the  proximity of a bunker in torino then on  the piazza de rizorgimento there's still  an active shelter capable of  accommodating  1150 people though during the war it  happened to welcome twice as many people  just as in naples where the population  found refuge from bombing in the network  of 19th century tunnels built by the  bourbons famous in milan are shelter 87  under an elementary school  and the breda bunkers in the parkland  north  in rome mussolini and the savoya family  had their own bunkers with blackjack and  hookers today you won't exactly find  this luxury in the bunk around at the  park of villaada once a royal residence  wanted by king vittorio manuela iii you  will find instead an anonymous and  disturbing parking lot however mussolini  had two bunkers one under palazzo  venezia and another one at villa  torlonia both in rome but they were not  even completed  45 kilometers from rome in the meanders  of mount zerate in the proximity of the  town of santoreste you can find a vast  angle of underground tunnels long four  kilometers and designed to accommodate  the highest charges of the army these  tunnels were then partially converted  into a bomb shelter by nato during the  cold war yet if some ill-intentioned  nation wants to attack us we should  expect more than anything else a direct  bombing towards military installations  such as aviano and getty with  consequences that nuke map itself  refuses to consider  i sincerely apologize if i too have  provided you with a daily dose of atomic  anxiety just in case remember your  potassium iodide pills for radiation and  map in your hand to calculate the damage  and the probability of survival a small  advice don't simulate the explosion of  the tar bomb the most powerful ever  built and designed by russia you may  experience nightmares  see you in the next video ciao

